# "Show me the weather" against the FAKE cloud (test/EXPECTED.md, SH13). The fake cloud asks the walker to
# show_on_screen the weather; the walker fills the card from its SIMULATED GPS and SIMULATED weather sample
# (--gps: no internet), puts it on the screen and returns its result; the fake cloud relays that result.
# The walker offers the screen only while a page is connected, so a browser must have the page open.
# Run (from devices/pi), with a headless browser on the printed http://127.0.0.1:8740/:
#   node dist/walker.mjs simulate --screen --gps --script test/sim/show-weather.walk
# test/show.test.ts also runs this file on a fake clock.

# Boot, and give the page time to connect.
expect spoke Sophi is on.
expect link online
expect screen ambient
wait 4000

# Ask: the card shows over "One moment" and the captions, and the answer relays the walker's result.
key show-weather
key t
expect screen listening
wait 1500
key t
expect screen showing
expect spoke Fake cloud: Showing the weather on the screen: Simulated weather, not a real forecast: 64 degrees

# The card stays SCREEN_SHOW_MS (30 s) after the answer has played, then the clock comes back.
absent 25000 screen ambient
expect 15000 screen ambient
key q
